        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="material, obsolete" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="Inventory refers to the production of  1 kg wool respectively live weight. The multioutput-process 'sheep' delivers the co-products 'wool, at farm' (4.2kg/head and year) and 'sheep live weight, at farm' (62.8 kg/head and year). Economic allocation with allocation factor of 22.8% to wool (exceptions see report).;&#10;UUID: 624a141e-d314-300f-a4c8-495e4566a906" includedProcesses="The inventory includes the processes of sheep husbandry on pasture land. Machine infrastructure and a shed for machine sheltering and shearing is included. Inputs of fertilisers, feedstuffs, pesticides and irrigation as well as transports to the farm are considered. The direct emissions on the field are also included. The system boundary is at the farm gate. The products of sheep husbandry are wool and sheep live weight. All further processes after the farm gate like transport to the slaughterhouse, slaughtering, cooling, etc. are excluded. " infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="material, obsolete" localName="xx Sheep for slaughtering, live weight, at farm" localSubCategory="agricultural, obsolete\animal production, obsolete" name="xx Sheep for slaughtering, live weight, at farm" subCategory="agricultural, obsolete\animal production, obsolete" unit="kg"/>
